-- VanillaDroid's own interface texts, in English (the default language). One file per area of the interface
-- (common, inventory, combat, social, travel...): every *.lang of this folder is read.
--
-- Same syntax as the client's Interface\FrameXML\GlobalStrings.lua: one KEY = "text"; per line, -- comments,
-- escapes \n \" \\ and \ddd. Baked into app.vdpk ("ui/strings/<locale>") by `vd_baker bake --only app`, which
-- travels inside the APK: a change here needs no re-bake of the player's packs (phase 22, ADR-0005).
--
-- Rules:
--  * Code never writes a text the player reads: it asks core/Text for a key (text::get, text::format).
--  * When the original client has the text, use its key from GlobalStrings.lua / GlueStrings.lua (ERR_INV_FULL,
--    LOOT_ITEM_SELF, SPELLLOGSELFOTHER...): it is already there, worded as the original, in the client's language.
--    Do not copy it here.
--  * Only what this client alone has (touch controls, mobile settings...) goes here, with a VD_ key in English.
--  * Formats use the client's specifiers: %s %d %u %c %.1f, and positional %1$s when a translation reorders them.
--  * A key may also be redefined here to fix a client text; other languages translate in locale/<locale>/*.lang.


